WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 10.4 · Legal, Compliance, Policies & Risk
Core policies: conduct, conflicts and anti-fraud

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
A few short core policies make expected behaviour and reporting routes clear.

3
00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:15.600
1. Cover conduct, conflicts of interest, fraud and harassment.

4
00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:18.200
2. Name an owner, a reporting route and consequences.

5
00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:22.200
3. Collect declarations yearly and at the start of meetings.

6
00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:23.800
An example: Vanita Weavers Cooperative (Cooperative · member-owned, India)

7
00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:31.000
“Vanita: yearly interest register read at the general meeting; a member whose relative supplies yarn does not vote on yarn.”

8
00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:33.400
You outline your core policies and declarations.

9
00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:37.400
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

10
00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:42.000
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
